<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρό-μακτρον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cloth for wiping the
				hands, towel, napkin,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.64
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				502
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.3.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				87.8
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>: the Scythians used scalps as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρόμακτρα,</span> Hdt.l.c.: hence 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκυθιστὶ χ. ἐκκεκαρμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					473
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>head-cloth,</i> used by women, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hecat.
				358
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, and perhaps so in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.122
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. χρύσεον,</span> [Written 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρώμακτρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PRev.Laws</u>
					94.4
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PEnteux.</u>
				38.3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειρόμακτρον</span>
			<u>PCair.Zen.</u> Il.cc. <span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>:</div> -ω- might be due to 'contamination' with
		the root of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμόργ-νυμι.]</span></div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
